      "description": "Watch Chapecoense AF vs Bahia highlights and goals from Brasileirão on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 16, 2026. On 2026-08-16 , the football world turned its attention to a pulsating Serie A clash in Brazil as Chapecoense AF hosted Bahia . Fans were treated to a rollercoaster of emotions in a match where momentum shifted with every passing minute. A Dramatic Opening Half Bahia took the initiative early on, breaking the deadlock in the 13th minute. Alejo Veliz stepped up to the penalty spot and calmly slotted the ball home to give the visitors the lead. However, the joy was short-lived as Chapecoense fought back almost immediately. In the 19th minute, Giovanni Augusto capitalized on an assist from Yago to level the score, signaling the start of a frantic contest. Just as the teams seemed headed for the break on even terms, a stroke of bad luck hit the home side. In the 42nd minute, an own goal by Kauan saw the ball end up in his own net, gifting Bahia a 2-1 lead heading into the interval. It was a cruel blow for the hosts, but it set the stage for an even more explosive second half. Momentum Swings and a Six-Goal Conclusion The second half began with Chapecoense firing on all cylinders. Only three minutes after the restart, Marcinho found the back of the net following a brilliant setup by Giovanni Augusto . The game then entered a period of high-octane attacking football. Bahia regained the lead in the 65th minute through Nicolas Acevedo , assisted by Jean Lucas , but the hosts refused to surrender. In the 72nd minute, Tulio Eduardo struck the equalizer for Chapecoense , once again assisted by the tireless Giovanni Augusto . As the clock ticked down, the match grew increasingly physical. Tactical substitutions and a flurry of yellow cards for Mateo Sanabria , Camilo , and Erick Pulga highlighted the desperate search for a winner. Despite several late chances, the final whistle confirmed a 3-3 draw, leaving both sets of fans breathless after a true footballing spectacle."
